    "q-327570": {
      "dom_id": "step-q327570",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "A company’s employee count increased to $125%$ of last year’s total. Of these employees, $20%$ work remotely. What percentage of last year’s total now work remotely?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $x$ be the number of employees last year.\n\nWe're told that the total number increased to $125%$ of last year’s total. Thus, the current number of employees is $1.25x.$\n\nWe are also told that of these employees, $20%$ work remotely. So, the number of employees working remotely is\n\n$$\n0.20(1.25x)=0.25x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.25x$ represents $25%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $25%$ of last year’s employees now work remotely.",
